From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 09:29:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 081/119] scene-referred S4: the output transform, and
 FilmMapping's other half

%_RT_SAMPLE0 - the permutation S2 already claimed for the pre-curve sun-shaft composite - now
also selects the whole body of FilmMapping. The two halves share the vignette scalar and the
bloom composite and nothing else.

The scene-referred half, per pixel:

    vignette x bloom composite      (shared; exposure is 1.0, S1 applied it on the light side)
    Bradford white balance 3x3      (CPU-computed constant, exactly identity when off)
    ACEScg -> ACEScct               (CommonMath.cfi's analytic shaper)
    ASC CDL: (in*slope + offset)^power, then saturation about the AP1 luminance
    LMT 3D fetch (t3)               (skipped when the slot is empty - D10's pure ACES default)
    ODT 3D fetch (t4)               -> display-encoded [0,1]
    dither                          (shared, unchanged)

and nothing else: no ComputeExposure (the whole-body #if is what keeps the EV formula and the
luminance fetch from being evaluated for a value this path throws away), no Hable curve, no sRGB
encode - the ODT carries it, because the back buffer is R8G8B8A8_UNORM and not sRGB-typed - and
no colour chart, which D9 skips whole.

- The CDL order is the ASC specification's: slope, then offset, then power on the clamped result,
  per channel, no cross-channel term; saturation is the ASC's own extension, after the SOP and
  about the luminance of the graded value. The luminance weights are AP1's, not Rec.709's,
  because that is the space this happens in.
- The half-texel inset for an N^3 grid is spelled out in SampleLut3D rather than folded into the
  call: getting it wrong is a small, uniform, entirely invisible error.
- The LUT helper lives in HDRPostProcess.cfx and not in PostEffectsLib.cfi. The research note
  suggested the shared header; there is exactly one consumer, and putting it there would
  invalidate the compiled form of every shader that includes it for no gain. Noted as a
  deviation.
- Six new float4s (SceneWBRow0..2, SceneCDLSlope/Offset/Power) rather than re-purposing
  HDRMiscParams: DisplayDebugInfo() still prints that block by its old meanings.
- With no ODT loaded the branch returns the clamped log image - visibly, unmistakably wrong -
  instead of falling back to the film curve and producing a plausible picture from a broken
  configuration (D13).
- White balance is the CAMERA'S setting: a Bradford adaptation FROM the set temperature TOWARDS
  the neutral one, so 3200 K in daylight reads blue. CCT -> xy is Kim et al.'s cubic on the
  Planckian locus; tint is a Duv offset perpendicular to it in the CIE 1960 UCS, positive =
  magenta. The neutral white is 6500 K + tint 0 through THAT SAME locus, not a tabulated D65, so
  the neutral setting is an exact identity by construction rather than an identity to six
  decimals.
- Eight new bus params carry the grade (bypass, WB enable/Kelvin/tint, slope/offset/power,
  saturation), all neutral by default. Nothing writes them yet - the camera controls are S5.

Also in this commit, because it invalidates the permutation cache anyway: the dead SAMPLE2 set
is gone. It was written for a vignette gate whose polarity was inverted years ago and that the
strength constant replaced; nothing has read the flag since. Every cached HDRFinalPass variant is
invalidated, the stock ones included, and not one pixel moves on either path.

